"""How serious each built-in finding is, and what we tell the owner about it (plain language, no jargon).

One table is the single source of severity for the configuration checks, so the rating is predictable and testable.
Rules of thumb (shown to the user in the README):
  critical - an attacker can take over or read everything with little effort (confirmed only)
  high     - a serious weakness, or something that should never be public
  medium   - a real weakness that needs another step to be abused
  low      - hardening that is missing
  info     - good to know; not counted in the score
"""

